  "ribbon_circuit_boundary": {
    "status": "passed",
    "formal_coverage": "Partial. Lean reduces the actual finite matroid of an arbitrary nonempty connected ribbon to a rank-preserving circuit matroid with the same Z-polynomial.",
    "scope": [
      "A splice of two bases of the contraction at an interior interval element is again a basis. The splice splits the matroid across the cut.",
      "For each required flat pair, explicit independent chains prove that both sides of the further contraction have positive rank.",
      "Each interior deletion preserves Z. Finite induction leaves exactly the separators, and each boundary basis omits exactly one separator.",
      "Relabeling the two sides preserves the flat ranks and the Kazhdan–Lusztig coefficients used in the direct-sum vanishing theorem."
    ],
    "remaining": [
      "Evaluate the actual circuit Z-polynomial as Narayana and check the real-rootedness and simple-negative-root conclusions."
    ],
